19. Industry Tips

Conditional rendering is one of the most frequently used techniques in professional React applications. You'll see it everywhere:

🔐 Authentication (Login vs Dashboard)
🛒 E-commerce (In Stock vs Out of Stock)
💳 Subscription apps (Free vs Premium features)
📱 Social media (Follow/Unfollow buttons)
📊 Dashboards (Loading, Error, Success states)
🔔 Notifications (Show badge only when notifications exist)
🛡️ Role-based access (Admin, Editor, User)

Production Best Practices:

Keep conditions simple and readable.
Move complex logic outside JSX into variables or helper functions.
Split large conditional sections into smaller reusable components.
Use meaningful variable names like isLoggedIn, isLoading, and hasPermission.
